ntent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T00:52:24Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T00:52:24Z","body":"@syntaxerror247 @Alex2782 Instead of opting out, we need to update the Godot APIs we use to return the edge insets so that Godot apps can 'automatically' do the right thing. \n\nIs that a task covering this issue? If not, let's create one for tracking and aim to resolve it in 4.5.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2914543427/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2919407828","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106810#issuecomment-2919407828","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106810","id":2919407828,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uAqDU","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T13:31:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T13:49:20Z","body":"> we need to update the Godot APIs we use to return the edge insets so that Godot apps can 'automatically' do the right thing.\r\n\r\nSomeone posted a GdScript solution for this on Reddit two days ago. Maybe we can simplify it.\r\nhttps://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1kwn26y/finally_made_the_system_bars_in_android/\r\n\r\non `godot-proposals`, the following question must be answered:\r\n`Is there a reason why this should be core and not an add-on in the asset library?`\r\n\r\nWill \"simplify\" be accepted as an answer for an API update? \r\n\r\nI think it would also have to be coordinated with iOS, which would be another good reason for an API update. \r\n_(unification / consolidation)_\r\n\r\n-----------\r\n\r\nOver 6 months ago I added the following link to my todo notes: \r\nhttps://developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/layout/edge-to-edge\r\n\r\nHowever, I can't remember if there's already an issue report or proposal for this. (I couldn't find anything after a brief search.)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2919407828/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2921942349","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106810#issuecomment-2921942349","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106810","id":2921942349,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uKU1N","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T10:25:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T10:25:47Z","body":"> > we need to update the Godot APIs we use to return the edge insets so that Godot apps can 'automatically' do the right thing.\r\n> \r\n> Someone posted a GdScript solution for this on Reddit two days ago. Maybe we can simplify it. https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1kwn26y/finally_made_the_system_bars_in_android/\r\n\r\nThis is to enable edge-to-edge mode in apps. I think, @m4gr3d means to say that Godot apps can automatically handle the edge to edge mode i.e prevent the app elements to get obstruct by the system bars. However, I believe that users should handle it themselves. Using JavaClassWrapper it's really easy to check the SDK version and update their app layout accordingly.\r\n```\r\nvar sdk_version = JavaClassWrapper.wrap(\"android.os.Build$VERSION\")\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2921942349/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2921958134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106810#issuecomment-2921958134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106810","id":2921958134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uKYr2","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T10:31:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T10:31:59Z","body":"@Alex2782 Regarding having an option to enable edge-to-edge, I have an easy to use [plugin](https://github.com/syntaxerror247/godot-android-system-bar-color-changer) for it which uses gdscript method in 4.4+, doesn't require gradle build and kotlin in older versions with gradle. A while ago, I had proposed this to @m4gr3d for adding this to core. Decision was to keep this as a plugin due to it being an Android specific things with no similar api on other platforms and can be easily done using a plugin.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2921958134/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]